     9	The Concrete-owned code is `main` (the runtime entry), `concrete_rt_write_all` and the body
    10	(`concrete_body`), with or without the Mach-O underscore. From `main`'s entry, every path through
    11	them is followed over the control-flow graph, tracking the stack pointer's depth below its value
    12	at `main`'s entry (and the frame pointer's). The bound is the deepest point reached, by the stack
    13	pointer or by any byte addressed relative to it or the frame pointer (the red zone below the
    14	stack pointer is used without moving it), counting each
    15	internal callee's own bound and the depth at which each external function (libc's `write`,
    16	`_exit`, `abort`) is entered; the external functions' own use is outside it (a premise, listed),
    17	and so is that `_exit` and `abort` do not return (a path ends at a call to one).
